    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking positive one-hundredth roots gives \\(n^2\\lt5^3=125.\\) Since \\(11^2=121\\lt125\\) but \\(12^2=144\\gt125,\\) the largest possible integer is \\(11.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
